WEBVTT

00:01.520 --> 00:04.100
<b>Rigarden Magical Academy</b>

00:02.190 --> 00:03.690
7,200.

00:04.430 --> 00:07.630
Of the 12,000 total credits
 available at the academy,

00:07.630 --> 00:10.370
that is the number required for a student 
to advance to the Upper Institute,

00:10.370 --> 00:13.350
an absolute condition for
 becoming a Magia Vander.

00:20.600 --> 00:21.980
Crims Serbe!

00:34.020 --> 00:35.260
Stear Viola!

00:43.470 --> 00:47.520
Sion Ulster! Colette Loire! 
You both pass!

00:47.520 --> 00:50.020
<b>Sion Ulster</b>

00:47.520 --> 00:50.020
<b>9,889 credits</b>

00:50.020 --> 00:52.530
<b>Colette Loire</b>

00:50.020 --> 00:52.530
<b>7,340 credits</b>

01:02.200 --> 01:04.020
Come on. What are you doing?

01:04.020 --> 01:08.100
A student of our magical academy 
is planning to throw a punch at it?

01:08.100 --> 01:09.590
What happened to your wand?

01:15.970 --> 01:20.430
He can't use magic and 
he can't even scratch a golem.

01:20.430 --> 01:23.850
I'd expect nothing less of a book-learner, 
an eternal failure in spellwork!

01:27.040 --> 01:28.340
Sagius Leo.

01:44.450 --> 01:45.830
Zephyros Claw.

02:04.180 --> 02:07.390
<b>Lihanna Owenzaus</b>

02:04.350 --> 02:07.390
<b>10,100 credits</b>

02:05.220 --> 02:07.050
Lihanna Owenzaus!

02:08.030 --> 02:09.820
Wignall Lindor!

02:08.350 --> 02:11.150
<b>Wignall Lindor</b>

02:08.440 --> 02:11.150
<b>10,075 credits</b>

02:09.820 --> 02:10.840
You pass!

02:32.530 --> 02:33.620
Ice over.

02:42.910 --> 02:46.140
That Julius. He went 
and froze ours, too.

02:47.130 --> 02:49.710
Julius Reinberg. You pass!

02:47.140 --> 02:50.140
<b>Julius Reinberg</b>

02:47.220 --> 02:50.140
<b>10,048 credits</b>

02:50.930 --> 02:54.020
It seems that neither of you two 
have lost your skills.

02:54.360 --> 02:58.650
There's no reason that I should have. 
The time for revels already draws near.

02:59.160 --> 03:01.210
Lihanna. Wignall.

03:01.210 --> 03:03.160
I'll declare my intent 
for war now.

03:03.930 --> 03:08.910
With my newly acquired secret method, 
this time I will defeat the both of you.

03:13.620 --> 03:16.420
You will accept this in
place of a gauntlet, won't you?

03:27.900 --> 03:30.460
I look forward to it, Julius.

03:31.410 --> 03:34.690
Wow. No wonder it's already confirmed 
they're going to the Upper Institute.

03:34.690 --> 03:37.780
Miss Perfect and the elf, 
Master Wignall.

03:38.390 --> 03:43.030
The only ones with over ten thousand 
credits are those two and Julius.

03:45.300 --> 03:49.690
<i>A student's credits are like an index by
 which their skills can be judged.</i>

03:50.490 --> 03:55.290
<i>I don't have enough to graduate, 
let alone advance to the Upper Institute.</i>

03:53.120 --> 03:58.170
<b>Will Serfort</b>

03:53.120 --> 03:58.170
<b>5,405 credits</b>

03:55.770 --> 03:58.800
<i>And this is my last year in school.</i>

04:07.970 --> 04:10.060
You're in the way, laggard.

04:10.530 --> 04:12.560
Could you please not 
show yourself in my presence?

04:12.560 --> 04:14.870
I-I'm sorry, Julius!

04:16.110 --> 04:17.800
You passed with just 
one spell again today!

04:17.800 --> 04:19.820
It's no wonder you're one of 
our year's top three!

04:20.120 --> 04:23.320
You're sure to get scouted 
at the Grand Magic Festival!

04:24.260 --> 04:27.160
Oh, right. It's already 
that time again.

05:51.280 --> 05:55.370
Episode 4
The Eve of the Grand Festival

06:00.840 --> 06:03.000
What are the odds of 
winning this year's Sky Race?

06:03.860 --> 06:07.720
I've already given up on that. 
I'm focused on the Dual Duel.

06:05.070 --> 06:08.220
You'll just have to get scouted at the
 Grand Magic Festival, too, Will!

06:07.720 --> 06:10.660
The rumor is that the elf faction 
is prioritizing those

06:08.220 --> 06:09.410
What?

06:09.450 --> 06:14.850
Well, advancing to the Upper Institute on 
Writing and Praxis alone just isn't realistic!

06:10.660 --> 06:12.840
who rank highly in Magic Craft.

06:12.840 --> 06:16.740
Elves are really conscious of only 
associating with other elves, so I don't know.

06:15.370 --> 06:17.480
And even with less than 
7,200 credits,

06:16.740 --> 06:19.560
I'm gonna make up for everything 
I messed up in Writing lessons!

06:17.480 --> 06:21.800
there's a precedent for a student being 
scouted and ascending the Tower on the spot.

06:22.650 --> 06:24.800
Well, you do have a point.

06:26.050 --> 06:28.350
<i>Though, around the time 
of the Grand Magic Festival,</i>

06:28.350 --> 06:31.600
<i>everyone's trying to turn things around 
with one shot, so they're all out for blood.</i>

06:35.030 --> 06:36.250
<i>The Grand Magic Festival.</i>

06:36.910 --> 06:41.180
<i>It's an event held by Rigarden 
Magical Academy once every two years.</i>

06:41.950 --> 06:44.820
<i>A number of different 
competitions are held,</i>

06:44.820 --> 06:48.710
<i>and High Mages come down 
from the tower as scouts.</i>

06:52.490 --> 06:53.940
Now, Will.

06:53.940 --> 06:55.860
The Grand Magic Festival is, in effect,

06:55.860 --> 06:58.560
a contest between students 
from the different Tower factions.

06:58.560 --> 07:02.170
You could even say that this is 
where advancement to the Tower is decided.

07:04.540 --> 07:08.380
The factions are the Lightning 
Lord's Wand, Thorzeus Fasce,

07:05.770 --> 07:08.190
Lightning Lord

07:08.930 --> 07:11.720
the Sacred Elf's Wand, 
Elleaf Caanan,

07:09.150 --> 07:11.570
Sacred Elf

07:12.390 --> 07:15.700
the Flame Emperor's Wand, 
Incindia Barham,

07:12.530 --> 07:14.950
Flame Emperor

07:15.700 --> 07:18.550
the Icemaiden's Wand, 
Albis Vina,

07:15.870 --> 07:18.330
Icemaiden

07:19.560 --> 07:22.820
and setting aside the 
Light Sovereign's Wand, Masterias Noah,

07:22.820 --> 07:25.760
the current Magia Vander 
lead these four major factions.

07:26.450 --> 07:28.580
If one of those factions 
chooses you,

07:28.580 --> 07:30.840
then your admittance as a 
Tower member is assured!

07:31.450 --> 07:33.800
Skipping the requirements for graduation

07:33.800 --> 07:36.600
and going straight to the 
Tower hardly ever happens.

07:36.600 --> 07:41.230
I'd have to perform some kind of magic 
that would put a High Mage's to shame.

07:41.710 --> 07:43.730
But that's not all!

07:44.060 --> 07:46.580
They say that people called Watchers 
appear at the Grand Magic Festival,

07:46.580 --> 07:50.340
snatch up outstanding talents, 
and carry them off to the Tower!

07:52.110 --> 07:56.190
Watchers? That's just one of the 
academy's seven legends, isn't it?

07:56.190 --> 07:59.400
A no-talent shouldn't try to stand out 
at the Grand Magic Festival.

07:59.400 --> 08:03.310
I'll work behind the scenes again this 
year. I'll help with operations.

08:04.170 --> 08:08.630
If you entered as you are now, Will, 
I think it would change the way people see you.

08:09.910 --> 08:15.260
Thank you, Colette. But if I entered, 
it would turn into a regular sports event.

08:15.900 --> 08:19.520
And when we were second-years, 
I had a really rough time because of that.

08:19.520 --> 08:21.280
Hey, that's cheating!

08:20.360 --> 08:21.770
Disqualify him!

08:21.280 --> 08:22.420
Get out!

08:21.770 --> 08:22.960
Quit interfering!

08:22.420 --> 08:23.520
Go away!

08:24.130 --> 08:27.880
The 50th Festival, also known as 
the absolute worst in history.

08:27.880 --> 08:30.200
Yes, that was quite something.

08:31.220 --> 08:33.270
That year, I stood out 
for all the wrong reasons.

08:33.700 --> 08:35.800
I feel like I'm still not over it.

08:45.850 --> 08:47.580
That's Magic Craft.

08:49.290 --> 08:51.340
And over there is Guardian Summoning.

08:52.420 --> 08:56.210
It really makes you feel how close 
the Grand Magic Festival is now.

08:56.210 --> 08:57.050
Yes.

08:57.360 --> 09:01.700
And a lot of scouts from other capitals 
besides Rigarden will be coming.

09:01.700 --> 09:06.190
Even if we can't ascend the Tower, 
there are still other paths you could follow!

09:06.190 --> 09:08.940
The Grand Magic Festival 
really is the perfect opportunity

09:08.940 --> 09:12.110
to show your abilities to others.

09:13.570 --> 09:17.200
And that's why you have to 
promote yourself, too, Will!

09:17.200 --> 09:21.590
I've told you already. 
I can't even use magic.

09:29.570 --> 09:31.210
Colette? Is something wrong?

09:37.340 --> 09:40.640
It's well hidden, but a 
barrier's been cast here.

09:40.640 --> 09:43.220
What? Not lock magic?

09:43.480 --> 09:47.010
An inhibitor...
and a sound-dampening barrier.

09:47.010 --> 09:50.180
I think I could probably use magic 
to break it by force, but...

09:50.610 --> 09:51.680
Kiki.

09:53.360 --> 09:54.410
What do you think?

10:00.030 --> 10:00.870
You did it!

10:00.870 --> 10:03.040
You're amazing, Kiki!

10:08.880 --> 10:11.360
A... A hidden stairway?

10:12.750 --> 10:15.750
I can hear something. Let's go!

10:16.260 --> 10:21.140
Now, step right up! Who will win 
each event at the Grand Magic Festival?

10:21.140 --> 10:23.010
We've got big predictions right now!

10:23.010 --> 10:24.600
Place your bets! Place your bets!

10:24.600 --> 10:25.840
Three hundred on Julius!

10:25.840 --> 10:27.630
Five hundred on Master Wignall!

10:27.630 --> 10:29.270
Eight hundred on Lihanna!

10:35.280 --> 10:37.580
U-Underground gambling?

10:37.580 --> 10:38.780
I can't believe them.

10:38.780 --> 10:42.440
Just because the professors 
don't come near the lockers,

10:42.440 --> 10:44.660
it's no reason to get up to all this.

10:48.790 --> 10:49.860
Sion?

10:50.620 --> 10:51.790
The laggard?

10:53.960 --> 10:55.920
Why are you here?

10:57.450 --> 10:59.400
We just happened to 
end up here.

10:59.400 --> 11:01.890
Now, stop being violent, Sion.

11:02.270 --> 11:07.640
The next time you're rough with Will for 
no reason, I will get seriously angry with you.

11:08.790 --> 11:12.680
U-Um, Sion, why are you here?

11:12.680 --> 11:15.710
It doesn't look like 
you've been gambling.

11:15.710 --> 11:16.900
What does it matter?

11:17.220 --> 11:21.150
That's right! It's not like he's 
wondering about the betting odds!

11:21.150 --> 11:25.860
Indeed! Word is, there's quite a spread 
between him, Lihanna, and the others.

11:25.860 --> 11:27.100
How frustrating!

11:27.100 --> 11:30.180
But Sion would never 
be thinking anything like that!

11:30.180 --> 11:33.380
I'm so sad because the top three 
don't even notice me!

11:33.380 --> 11:35.560
That's a thought that'd 
never cross his mind!

11:36.040 --> 11:38.420
You two, just stop talking!

11:41.680 --> 11:44.180
Sorry, Sion!

11:44.180 --> 11:47.880
My! Are you concerned 
about Lihanna and the others?

11:47.880 --> 11:50.430
Well, you are a boy 
after all, Sion.

11:50.780 --> 11:53.000
I'm not particularly concerned.

11:53.470 --> 11:56.060
It isn't as if they've beaten me.

11:56.450 --> 12:00.690
And the number of credits I lag behind them 
are simply credits I lost in Writing exams.

12:01.240 --> 12:03.820
I've been training ever since that day.

12:04.330 --> 12:07.550
In terms of magical skill, 
I'm just as good as Lihanna and Wignall.

12:07.550 --> 12:09.300
Look how high you are!

12:10.360 --> 12:13.590
Why am I explaining myself to you?

12:16.510 --> 12:17.930
Hey, Sion!

12:17.930 --> 12:18.780
Sion!

12:18.780 --> 12:19.880
Wait for us!

12:20.370 --> 12:22.880
<i>A festival held once 
every two years.</i>

12:22.880 --> 12:27.300
<i>I suppose it's no wonder 
everyone is so excited about it.</i>

12:32.280 --> 12:34.010
That's all for today!

12:34.010 --> 12:37.650
Next time, we will actually 
craft some magic potions.

12:37.650 --> 12:40.350
Be sure to review the material 
and prepare for the lesson.

12:42.250 --> 12:44.030
Kiki, it's over.

12:48.110 --> 12:49.120
Will!

12:49.530 --> 12:51.610
Um, what are you 
doing after this?

12:51.610 --> 12:53.500
If you're going to the 
dungeon, I'll go with you.

12:56.380 --> 12:57.740
Sorry, Colette!

12:57.740 --> 13:00.250
I'm working at Miss Gina's 
tavern tonight.

13:01.900 --> 13:03.750
Oh, honestly!

13:06.090 --> 13:07.590
Crystal for monitoring Will

13:07.910 --> 13:11.010
<b><u>Kiki

</u><b>The reason I gave Kiki to Will? 
Because that boy is always acting recklessly 
of course. If he doesn't at least have a 
talented familiar with him, I wouldn't 
feel comfortable watching him go into the
 dungeon. And that incident on the 6th floor
 the other day. If Kiki's crystal hadn't been 
connected to mine, I wouldn't have been 
able to see— That was a slip of the tongue. 
Please forget about it.


Workner Norgram</b></b>

13:13.350 --> 13:16.020
<u><b>Dwarves

<b></b></b></u>Short in stature with short limbs. Also, 
they reek of sweat. What else is there 
to know? They're deft with their hands
 and they have insane physical strength? 
You fool. If one has magic, one doesn't
 need any of that. 

A certain mage who believes in 
the absolute rule of magic

13:17.230 --> 13:20.650
<i>Slumland Street is on the
 outskirts of Urbus Rigarden.</i>

13:17.350 --> 13:20.650
<b>Slumland Street</b>

13:17.560 --> 13:20.650
<b>Urbus Rigarden
Outskirts of the Capital of Magic</b>

13:20.650 --> 13:23.400
<b>Gina's Tavern
The Hen and Beanstalk</b>

13:23.400 --> 13:28.200
<i>Today, like every day, the exploited 
miners quaff their alcohol.</i>

13:28.200 --> 13:31.660
<i>The sound of laughter rings out
 through this dwarven bystreet.</i>

13:34.300 --> 13:35.960
Will, take this out!

13:35.960 --> 13:38.420
One goulard bean 
sautée, order up!

13:38.420 --> 13:40.220
Coming, Miss Gina!

13:41.550 --> 13:43.720
Put your back into it, Will!

13:45.910 --> 13:48.240
Mister Donnan, 
thank you for waiting.

13:48.690 --> 13:51.140
Oh, thanks, Will.

13:51.810 --> 13:54.680
You've got it pretty 
rough too, don't you?

13:54.680 --> 13:58.020
Newspaper delivery in the mornings. 
Student during the day.

13:58.020 --> 14:00.640
Then waiting tables 
for Gina at night.

14:02.190 --> 14:04.730
I'm not eligible for a scholarship,

14:04.730 --> 14:07.070
so if I don't work, 
I won't be able to pay my tuition.

14:09.390 --> 14:11.320
That reminds me, 
it's coming up soon, isn't it?

14:11.970 --> 14:13.320
What's it called again?

14:13.320 --> 14:15.680
That's right! The Grand Magic Festival.

14:15.680 --> 14:18.080
If you're in that, 
couldn't that fix things for you?

14:18.080 --> 14:21.590
Oh, no, no, no! I really couldn't enter that!

14:22.620 --> 14:25.090
Quit chatting and work, Will!

14:25.090 --> 14:26.240
Yikes!

14:26.240 --> 14:28.970
Your buddy is working much harder than you!

14:30.070 --> 14:32.830
Table three, thank you for waiting!

14:33.500 --> 14:35.180
Thanks!

14:35.890 --> 14:37.560
I'll have another ale!

14:37.560 --> 14:39.980
Of course, coming right up!

14:42.500 --> 14:44.110
Whoops!

14:44.110 --> 14:46.630
Sorry for asking you 
to help out like this, Rosty.

14:47.090 --> 14:50.520
Working without using magic is a fun 
new experience. Don't worry about it.

14:50.520 --> 14:53.530
Besides, my roommate 
was in a bind, right?

14:54.260 --> 14:56.650
One of my staff went and quit.

14:56.650 --> 14:59.620
Bring me another part-timer, 
won't you, Will?

15:00.630 --> 15:05.080
What're you talking about, Miss Gina? 
This lad'll work as hard as two!

15:05.080 --> 15:06.740
Will can do it!

15:06.740 --> 15:07.780
What?

15:07.780 --> 15:10.540
Because you're a
 brother to us dwarves, right?

15:12.510 --> 15:15.830
Everyone, please don't do this to me!

15:18.870 --> 15:21.300
But Will, are you all right with this?

15:21.300 --> 15:22.200
With what?

15:22.890 --> 15:26.780
The wages the dwarves 
pay you aren't high, right?

15:26.780 --> 15:31.600
Professor Workner would be able to 
help you find a better job, wouldn't he?

15:32.030 --> 15:35.530
I'm already making all sorts of
 trouble for Professor Workner.

15:37.550 --> 15:38.540
Besides...

15:39.030 --> 15:42.990
Mister Donnan and the others...
I like them. I like the dwarves.

15:44.060 --> 15:46.510
They're a hearty people. 
They love alcohol.

15:46.510 --> 15:48.300
And they're really skilled 
with their hands!

15:48.770 --> 15:52.000
Despite me being like this, 
they've welcomed me warmly.

15:53.140 --> 15:55.790
I respect the dwarves.

15:56.570 --> 15:57.620
I see.

16:15.900 --> 16:18.140
What sort of vulgar tavern is this?

16:18.140 --> 16:21.830
Sorry, Julius! None of the 
other taverns are open.

16:25.380 --> 16:27.590
Will, isn't he from the academy?

16:32.360 --> 16:33.720
Is that the laggard?

16:35.340 --> 16:39.280
Come now. Don't tell me 
you work here?

16:42.010 --> 16:43.680
Well, this is beautiful!

16:44.100 --> 16:47.110
The no-talent and the barbarians. 
You suit each other perfectly!

16:47.110 --> 16:48.850
What did you just say?

16:48.850 --> 16:50.110
H-Hey.

16:55.390 --> 16:58.240
What is it, dwarf? 
What's that look in your eye?

16:58.840 --> 17:02.120
You're an inferior race that 
immigrated here from another world.

17:02.600 --> 17:06.250
You're being allowed to live in 
this country by the grace of others.

17:06.830 --> 17:08.380
Know your place!

17:15.610 --> 17:21.140
<i>Long ago, when the dwarves' world 
was destroyed by the Celestial Host,</i>

17:21.450 --> 17:23.530
<i>they escaped to our world.</i>

17:24.420 --> 17:26.480
This is a tavern, isn't it?

17:26.480 --> 17:28.650
Hurry up and bring me 
food and drink!

17:29.170 --> 17:33.110
<i>Unlike the elves, 
dwarves are treated with disdain.</i>

17:33.530 --> 17:37.900
<i>Were a dwarf to lay hands on a mage, 
their standing would instantly be in danger.</i>

17:38.930 --> 17:41.610
<i>In this world, magic rules absolute.</i>

17:42.050 --> 17:45.240
<i>The discrimination against dwarves 
shows the world in microcosm.</i>

17:46.610 --> 17:47.510
<i>Still...</i>

17:53.110 --> 17:55.670
What is this bean dish?

17:55.670 --> 17:59.040
Even out in the countryside 
they can serve up better food than this!

17:59.040 --> 18:01.430
What's wrong with these
 barbarians' sense of taste?

18:05.870 --> 18:09.690
More than anything else, it reeks. 
It's difficult to endure this stench of sweat.

18:09.970 --> 18:10.970
<i>Still...</i>

18:12.090 --> 18:14.930
Even beasts are better 
than these filthy brutes.

18:14.930 --> 18:17.830
Hurry up and get out of our country!

18:20.930 --> 18:21.850
<i>Will?</i>

18:26.010 --> 18:27.000
<i>Still...</i>

18:32.060 --> 18:33.750
What is it, no-talent?

18:33.750 --> 18:35.760
We didn't call for a server.

18:38.100 --> 18:40.600
I want you to take back those insults.

18:42.500 --> 18:43.700
What did you say?

18:44.510 --> 18:49.540
The dwarves' beans, grown from barren soil, 
are the culmination of the dwarves' wisdom!

18:50.020 --> 18:54.620
The dwarves' sweat is proof of their 
earnest toil under the harshest conditions!

18:55.620 --> 18:58.390
They are not things which 
should ever be sneered at!

19:03.590 --> 19:07.540
Since none of you can use magic, 
do you sit around licking each other's wounds?

19:07.540 --> 19:09.160
If something reeks, it reeks.

19:09.690 --> 19:12.290
If something's an eyesore 
I'll call it an eyesore.

19:12.290 --> 19:13.790
What's wrong with that?

19:26.060 --> 19:28.180
Don't get any ideas, no-talent!

19:28.180 --> 19:29.930
Hurry up and get out of our sight!

19:47.340 --> 19:49.860
The savagery between you and me

19:49.860 --> 19:54.080
is far more senseless than that of
 the dwarves. We're worse than beasts.

19:59.390 --> 20:02.340
I haven't faced humiliation 
like this in a while.

20:07.320 --> 20:11.980
You understand who you've just 
picked a fight with, don't you?

20:14.480 --> 20:16.360
No-talent!

20:32.620 --> 20:33.750
Pin him in place.

21:00.740 --> 21:02.280
Hey, that's going too far!

21:14.920 --> 21:16.840
I've changed my mind.

21:18.330 --> 21:21.570
Encasing you in ice here 
won't be enough to appease me.

21:24.020 --> 21:26.440
Enter the Grand Magic Festival, no-talent!

21:26.860 --> 21:30.830
I will humiliate you 
in front of all of those spectators!

21:37.640 --> 21:39.810
All right. I'll enter.

21:40.250 --> 21:41.690
W-Wait, Will!

21:42.700 --> 21:43.820
<i>It's no good.</i>

21:44.370 --> 21:46.190
<i>He's seriously angry.</i>

21:46.970 --> 21:51.580
I will win and remove any space for you 
to belong within the academy!

21:51.950 --> 21:55.760
If I win, please apologize to
 Mister Donnan and the others.

